# Plan → build (dsh)

Ordinary authorized work stays in the current session: plan, perform, and
verify it there. Run PB only when David explicitly asks for it or confirms a
router recommendation. That explicit PB request needs the configured OpenAI
Planner → Builder route; dsh cannot dispatch it, so it must fail closed rather
than claim a disciplined current-session pass used the configured models.

Await the Planner's terminal output before starting Builder; never pre-spawn
Builder. Use one Planner and one Builder per round. At most one plan-authorized
L1/FE delegation is allowed; multi-workstream work requires an explicit Team
Leader call.

